Pulupulu builds on two open-source projects. Their ideas, rule texts, and
command playbooks were merged, rewritten, and extended here. Pulupulu's
detector, browser checks, hook, and installer are original code.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
antislop (Anti Slop: Rules for AI Coding Agents)
https://github.com/miqdadbadjuber/anti-slop
Copyright (c) 2026 Miqdad Badjuber
Licensed under the MIT License. Full text: LICENSES/antislop-MIT.txt

Used: rule set R-01 to R-38 and its numbering, the three rule tiers, the
Craftsmanship Standard, the Liveliness dials, the Delivery Gate, the
during/after modes, and the UI, copywriting, human, mobile-layout, and
code-comment guidance. All were edited and extended.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Impeccable
https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable
Copyright 2025 Paul Bakaus
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Full text: LICENSES/impeccable-Apache-2.0.txt

Used: the surface modes (Persuade, Operate, Read, Experience), the craft
floor checks, the command vocabulary and playbook structure, the PRODUCT.md
and DESIGN.md split, and the idea of deterministic detector rules with an
edit-time hook. All were condensed and rewritten; the detector is a new
JavaScript implementation, not a port of Impeccable's engine.
